<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="csrf-token" content={get_csrf_token()} />
    <.live_title default="BIAB Phoenix starter">{assigns[:page_title]}</.live_title>
    <link phx-track-static rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/app.css"} />
    <%!--
      The <biab-form> stylesheet and the element itself come from esm.sh, not
      from this app's asset pipeline. That is the whole reason a Phoenix
      consumer never reimplements the form renderer: the component ships the
      conditional blocks, availability picker and upload handling, and talks
      only to this app's own /api/biab/forms proxy — so the bearer key stays
      on the server.

      Pinned to an exact version deliberately. A CDN import has no lockfile,
      so @latest would roll this page forward on somebody else's release.
    --%>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://esm.sh/@businessdash/sdk@0.9.60/biab-forms.css" />
    <script defer phx-track-static type="text/javascript" src={~p"/assets/app.js"}>
    </script>
    <script type="module">
      import { setBiabFormClient } from "https://esm.sh/@businessdash/sdk@0.9.60/element";
      setBiabFormClient({ baseUrl: "/api/biab/forms", apiKey: "browser-proxy" });
    </script>
  </head>
  <body>
    {@inner_content}
  </body>
</html>
